   - `src = zip_source_decompress(srcza, src, st.comp_method)` - creates decompress source wrapping the window source. `zip_source_layered_create` does NOT keep the window source. So the window source's refcount stays at 1 (from `_zip_source_new`).
   - `src = zip_source_crc_create(src, 1, error)` - creates CRC source wrapping the decompress source. Same - no keep.
   - Then `partial_data && needs_decompress` is true:
     - `s2 = _zip_source_window_new(src, start, data_len, &st2, 0, NULL, 0, error)` - creates another window source wrapping the CRC source. `_zip_source_window_new` calls `zip_source_layered_create` (no keep) and then `zip_source_keep(src)` (refcount of CRC source becomes 2)
     - `src = s2`

Now, the issue is in the `partial_data && (needs_decrypt || needs_decompress)` branch at the end:

```c
if (partial_data && (needs_decrypt || needs_decompress)) {
    ...
    s2 = _zip_source_window_new(src, start, data_len, &st2, 0, NULL, 0, error);
    if (s2 == NULL) {
        zip_source_free(src);
        return NULL;
    }
    src = s2;
}
```

Before the regression commit, this was:
```c
s2 = _zip_source_window_new(src, start, data_len, &st2, 0, NULL, 0, error);
zip_source_free(src);  // <-- this was removed
if (s2 == NULL) {
    return NULL;
}
src = s2;
```

The `zip_source_free(src)` was removed because the new ownership model says that `_zip_source_window_new` takes ownership of `src` (via `zip_source_layered_create` which no longer keeps, but `_zip_source_window_new` compensates by calling `zip_source_keep(src)`).

Wait, let me re-think. In the new model:
- `zip_source_layered_create` no longer calls `zip_source_keep(src)` - so the layered source does NOT increment the refcount of the lower source
- `_zip_source_window_new` compensates by calling `zip_source_keep(src)` after `zip_source_layered_create` - so the window source DOES increment the refcount of the lower source

So in `_zip_source_window_new`:
1. `zip_source_layered_create(src, ...)` creates a layered source with `zs->src = src` (no keep)
2. `zip_source_keep(src)` increments refcount of `src` to 2

This means the window source holds one reference to `src`, and the caller still holds one reference to `src`.

Now in `zip_source_zip_file_create`, the `partial_data && (needs_decrypt || needs_decompress)` branch:
